  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal, somewhat literary word used to describe the specific type of separation caused by someone's death. Takes と to mark the person one was separated from: ～と{死別|しべつ}する.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～と{死別|しべつ}する (to be parted from ~ by death)\n- {死別|しべつ}を{経験|けいけん}する (to experience bereavement)\n- {親|おや}との{死別|しべつ} (losing a parent to death)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {生|い}き{別|わか}れ: separation from a living person — being separated without death, typically due to circumstances\n- {別離|べつり}: separation; parting — literary term for separation in general",
